course: dictionary
lesson: 11932
title: A false story that keeps going round
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you that a story is not true. Read the sentence and look for clues. «The old canard that the school would close next week was repeated by everyone, but it was never true.» The words was repeated by everyone and but it was never true show you the story is false, so a canard must be a false story.
explain: A canard is a story or rumour that many people pass on and believe, often because someone spread it on purpose. Another way to check is to ask: is this a fact, or a story people keep repeating? If it keeps going round but has no proof, it may be a canard.
explain: The word also has other meanings. On a plane, a canard is a small extra wing near the front, in front of the main wings. In French, canard is the ordinary word for a duck, but in English we do not use it for the bird. Use the sentence around the word to know which meaning is meant.
fact: A canard is a false story or rumour that many people repeat and believe.
fact: A canard is often spread on purpose, so people can be fooled by it.
fact: Phrases you may see: an old canard, a tired canard, repeat a canard.
fact: On an aircraft, a canard is a small wing near the front of the plane.
fact: In French, canard means a duck, but in English it is not used for the bird.
exercise: «Everyone repeated the old canard that the school would close next week, but it was a lie.» What is a canard? | A kind of bird that lives on ponds | A true report in the newspaper | A small wing at the front of a plane | *A false story that many people repeat and believe
exercise: «The small plane had a canard near its nose.» What is the canard in this sentence? | A bird's nest | A tail at the back of the plane | A type of fuel | *A small extra wing near the front
exercise: «Ravi said the canard about bats being blind again, but he knew it was false.» What does the word canard tell the reader about the story? | The story is about a duck | *The story is false | The story is true | The story is very funny
test: Tom said, «Repeating a canard is like passing on a lie.» What does repeat a canard mean? | Count to ten slowly | Sing a song loudly | *Tell a false story again | Draw a picture of a duck
test: Which word is closest in meaning to canard? | Truth | Wing | *Myth | Duck
exam: «Mia spotted the tired canard in the newspaper, so she checked the facts before she believed it.» What does the sentence tell us about canard? | It is a kind of bird that lives on farms | *It is a false story that keeps going round | It is a part of a plane's engine | It is a fact that everyone knows is true
